{"name":"Light Sandbank","hex":"#dedcc6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"sandbank","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ridge of sand along a shore that is partially or totally submerged and thus a hazard to shipping."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandbank"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shoal","blocks":[{"text":"A shoal is a natural submerged ridge, bank, or bar that consists of, or is covered by, sand or other unconsolidated material, and rises from the bed of a body of water close to the surface or above it, which poses a danger to navigation. Shoals are also known in oceanography, geomorphology, and geoscience, as sandbanks, sandbars, gravelbars, or bars. Two or more shoals that are either separated by shared troughs or interconnected by past or present sedimentary and hydrographic processes are referred to as a shoal complex."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/GughSandbar.JPG/330px-GughSandbar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoal","wikidata":"Q28337"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/WayaWayasewa.jpg/500px-WayaWayasewa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/WayaWayasewa.jpg/500px-WayaWayasewa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A tidal sandbar connecting the islands of Waya and Wayasewa of the Yasawa Islands, Fiji","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWayaWayasewa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Nosy_Iranja_097.jpg/500px-Nosy_Iranja_097.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Nosy_Iranja_097.jpg/1280px-Nosy_Iranja_097.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Nosy_Iranja_097.jpg/500px-Nosy_Iranja_097.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sandbar between Nosy Iranja Be and Nosy Iranja Kely(Nosy Iranja, Madagascar)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANosy_Iranja_097.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/1_Amanohashidate_panorama_2014.jpg/500px-1_Amanohashidate_panorama_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/1_Amanohashidate_panorama_2014.jpg/1280px-1_Amanohashidate_panorama_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki